1	// In-process, time bounded lease registry with append-only log persistence
2	// and crash-safe snapshots. Time only moves when the injected clock moves;
3	// nothing expires on its own. Tokens are derived from the injected clock as
4	// well, never from wall time.
5	//
6	// Resources may be declared with a share capacity: several holders then
7	// occupy the same resource at once, each holding one credential per share
8	// with its own independent expiry. An undeclared resource stays a
9	// single-occupancy resource exactly as before. Hierarchical quotas sit above
10	// resources: a parent quota bounds the sum of the shares occupied under every
11	// quota below it (and directly declared resources), and every level is
12	// enforced at once.
13	//
14	// Every resource keeps a credential epoch, starting at 1 on its first grant
15	// and advanced by exactly one per committed credential (retake, same-holder
16	// reacquisition and woken grants included). Renewals never advance it, nor do
17	// failed, queued, timed-out, cancelled or partially committed requests; it
18	// never moves backwards and survives restarts and compactions. The newest
19	// credential of an exclusive resource is therefore the leader epoch, and
20	// assertLease is the fence a holder passes only while it still is that
21	// leader.
22	//
23	// Persistence layout:
24	//   <logPath>           append-only event log, one JSON object per line
25	//   <logPath>.snapshot  last compacted state image (single JSON line)
26	// Startup loads the snapshot (if any) and replays only the events past the
27	// compacted boundary marker. Compaction publishes both files through a
28	// temp-file + fsync + rename sequence, so a failure at any step leaves the
29	// previous snapshot and the previous log usable. Every event carries a
30	// monotonic sequence number; a snapshot found next to an un-exchanged
31	// original log (the log swap died after the snapshot rename) simply skips
32	// the already-folded events by their sequence ids, so each event applies
33	// exactly once regardless of which rename made it to disk.
34	
35	import fs from 'node:fs';
36	import path from 'node:path';
